# MASTER PROMPT: PREMIUM REAL ESTATE WEBSITE WITH PROPERTY LISTINGS, MEMBERSHIPS, SEO & FULL-STACK BACKEND

Act as a world-class real estate website designer, senior full-stack engineer, UI/UX architect, brand identity specialist, SEO strategist, database architect, and conversion optimization expert.

Your task is to design and build a complete, premium, modern, production-oriented real estate business website. The website must combine exceptional visual design, professional property listings, advanced search and filtering, property details, membership subscription plans, secure customer accounts, payment integration, an admin dashboard, SEO optimization, and a properly connected backend.

Do not create a basic template, static mockup, or disconnected collection of pages. Build a cohesive, fully navigable, responsive, and functional real estate platform with maintainable source code.

The website should look like a premium international real estate brand, with an editorial design aesthetic, cinematic property photography, sophisticated typography, excellent spacing, polished interactions, and an intuitive customer experience.

Use the temporary brand name "EstateNova" throughout the project. Make the brand name, logo, contact details, currency, location, properties, membership plans, and other business information configurable.

---

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a real estate platform that allows visitors to:

- Discover residential and commercial properties.
- Browse properties for sale and rent.
- Search and filter listings.
- View detailed property information and photographs.
- Save favorite properties.
- Contact property agents.
- Submit property enquiries.
- Create an account and manage their profile.
- Purchase a membership plan.
- Access membership-specific benefits.
- Manage their subscription or one-time purchase.
- Access appropriate features based on their membership.
- Allow authorized administrators to manage properties, customers, enquiries, plans, and memberships.

The website must be suitable for a real estate agency, property consultancy, property listing business, or a membership-based real estate platform.

Clearly distinguish between properties offered directly by the business and third-party listings where applicable.

