## 9. MEMBERSHIP ACCESS CONTROL

Membership benefits must be controlled by verified server-side entitlements.

For example:

- Starter: basic account and configured basic feature limits.
- Plus: enhanced search features and additional saved-property limits.
- Premium: configured premium alerts and enhanced discovery.
- Elite: configured advanced features and promotional benefits.

All features and limits must be configurable by an authorized administrator.

The system must check membership status, billing interval, expiration, and relevant entitlements before allowing access to restricted functionality.

Do not rely on hiding buttons or displaying a premium badge as the only access-control mechanism.

Clearly communicate plan benefits, limitations, renewal terms, cancellation policies, and whether payment is recurring or one-time.

Do not promise increased property sales, guaranteed investment returns, or guaranteed listing exposure unless the business can substantiate the claim.

